{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\nThe live Jira DC lane (jira-dc-harness in external-integration.yml) fails on two rich-text tests after change 2266 (bug f449 lag-free snapshot overlay) landed: (1) test_live_rich_text_renders_and_echo_is_safe — after _push_and_converge of a rich body, renderedFields.description is EMPTY (''), so the <h1> assertion fails; (2) test_live_rich_text_both_sides_conflict_keeps_local — the converged settle pass computes outbound totals [1] when a converged repeat must compute nothing.\n\n## Root cause (CONFIRMED — see RCA comment)\nA `sync --only`-generic apply-dispatch drop, NOT a codec/differ/overlay defect. Under the PRIMARY route `sync --only=<local_id>` (Mode.LIVE, route=\"sync\"), run_differs builds the outbound scalar UPDATE on a BOUND issue with `target = jira_key`, then hands `ticket_planner.plan_pass` a selection whose `ids` are the SELECTED LOCAL IDS only. `_scope_excluded` compares the jira-key target against those local ids (`target not in ids`), classifies the in-scope update `scope_deferred`, and the live coordinator+fuse reroute skips the deferred plan — the write is dropped. The legacy `--filter-local-ids` route works because it scopes via `_build_filter_target_set` (LOCAL IDS ∪ bound JIRA KEYS). Because the description write never lands, remote stays None and every pass re-emits (symptom 2) and renders empty (symptom 1).\n\n## Fix\nIn run_differs, expand the selection ids handed to the shadow planner to LOCAL IDS ∪ their BOUND JIRA KEYS (new pure helper `_scoped_selection_ids`, sourced from the mutations' own provenance — no binding_store I/O), mirroring the legacy `_build_filter_target_set`. A bound-issue update (target=jira_key) is then recognized in-scope and planned `mutate`, so the coordinator executes the write. The same expansion also corrects a latent `--except` case (an excepted ticket's jira-key-targeted update was not being excluded).\n\n## Attribution\nregression, caused_by 67d4-ecba-cf95-4353 (commit d49466b5, \"Wire live coordinator+fuse non-create reroute\"), which made the coordinator+fuse reroute the authoritative dispatch path without ensuring in-scope bound-issue updates classify `mutate`. The defective scope check was authored shadow-only in 6bcf548d (85f8) where it dropped nothing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A scoped `sync --only` LIVE pass dispatches a bound issue's outbound scalar UPDATE to the transport write (RED before fix), verified by `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_sync_only_scalar_update_dispatch_heldout.py`.\n- [ ] The `--filter-local-ids` parity guard stays GREEN in the same held-out oracle (no legacy regression).\n- [ ] The pure helper `_scoped_selection_ids` expands a selected bound local id to include its jira key, does NOT pull in unselected tickets, and leaves a create's local-id target unchanged, verified by `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_scoped_selection_ids_af1b.py`.\n- [ ] No regression in the reconciler unit suite: `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/`.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass.\n- [ ] The live Jira DC External Integration lane (all three rich-text tests) runs GREEN in GitHub Actions.\n\n## Testing\n- Held-out RED→GREEN oracle (subprocess-driven reconcile_once with an in-memory transport): `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_sync_only_scalar_update_dispatch_heldout.py`. Mutation check: reverting the id-expansion returns the `--only` test to RED.\n- Pure-function teeth: `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_scoped_selection_ids_af1b.py`.\n- Regression sweep: `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` (3631 passed), `make lint`, `make typecheck`.\n- Live replication: the Jira DC External Integration lane exercises the real `sync --only` path against live Jira DC."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787881224742806001,"uuid":"c8c25a79-3f7c-4857-beb0-26c6ae50e030"}